<LegalPage title="Notice of Privacy Practices" lede="This notice describes how medical information about you may be used and shared, and how you can get access to it. Please review it carefully." description="HIPAA Notice of Privacy Practices for Advanced Foot & Ankle Specialists of Arizona.">
  <p>We are required by federal law (HIPAA) to protect the privacy of your health information, to give you this notice, and to follow it.</p>

  <h2>How we may use and share your health information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Treatment:</strong> to care for you, for example sharing information with your primary doctor, a specialist, a lab, or a physical therapist.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment:</strong> to bill and collect payment from you, your insurance plan, or others responsible for your care.</li>
    <li><strong>Health care operations:</strong> to run our practice, check the quality of care, train staff, and meet legal duties.</li>
    <li><strong>Appointment reminders and follow-up:</strong> to contact you about visits and your care.</li>
    <li><strong>As required by law:</strong> for public health, abuse or neglect reports, health oversight, court orders, law enforcement, and other situations the law requires or permits.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For any other use, such as most marketing, or sharing psychotherapy notes, we need your written permission. You may cancel that permission in writing at any time.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>See and get a copy</strong> of your medical and billing records.</li>
    <li><strong>Ask for a correction</strong> if you think something is wrong or incomplete.</li>
    <li><strong>Ask for private communication</strong>, for example by a different phone number or address.</li>
    <li><strong>Ask us to limit</strong> how we use or share your information. We may say no, but if you pay for a service in full yourself, you may ask us not to share it with your health plan, and we will agree.</li>
    <li><strong>Get a list</strong> of certain times we shared your information.</li>
    <li><strong>Get a paper copy</strong> of this notice at any time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Our duties</h2>
  <p>We will keep your information private and secure. We will tell you if a breach puts your information at risk. We will follow the terms of this notice, and we may change it. If we do, the new notice applies to all information we hold, and we will post it in our office and on this website.</p>

  <h2>Questions or complaints</h2>
  <p>If you believe your privacy rights were violated, you may file a complaint with our office at <a href="tel:+14809639000">480-963-9000</a> or with the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services Office for Civil Rights at <a href="https://www.hhs.gov/hipaa/filing-a-complaint/" rel="noopener">hhs.gov/hipaa/filing-a-complaint</a>. We will not punish you for filing a complaint.</p>

  <p class="text-sm text-navy-900/55">Effective date: November 13, 2026.</p>
</LegalPage>
